-- Row il-67. TESTS OF THE CONTROLS: the sound references kept beside the defects. They pass.
-- Each control is a section the citing words name whose target is printed and untouched (or amended and still present) in the instruments read.
-- The expected values are hand-written from the quotation lines in tn67-cross-references.l4 and from the printed pages, not copied from the statuses there.

§ `Tests of the controls`

-- I1 control: section 49, named by the same citation as the repealed section 46.
#ASSERT `the section is in force` `section 49`

-- I2 control: section 45, named by the same citation as section 46.
#ASSERT `the section is in force` `section 45`

-- I3 control: section 45 is one of the numbers the range names, and it is in force.
#ASSERT elem 45 (`item I3: the range in section 48`'s `the numbers the range names`)
#ASSERT `the section is in force` `section 45`

-- I4 control: the sections that section 53 cites and the row checks, 52 and 52A, are in force; section 61 is not checked.
#ASSERT `the section is in force` `section 52`
#ASSERT `the section is in force` `section 52A`
#ASSERT `every section the citation names that the row checked is in force` `control to I4: section 53 cites sections 52, 52A and 61`
#ASSERT NOT (`some section the citation names is repealed` `control to I4: section 53 cites sections 52, 52A and 61`)
#ASSERT NOT (`every section the citation names is in force` `control to I4: section 53 cites sections 52, 52A and 61`)

-- The day a repeal took effect is not given by the pages read, so there is no answer.
#ASSERT `the day the repeal of the section took effect` `section 46` EQUALS NOTHING
